{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1548835","title":"Effects of different pretreatments whether sterilized or not on Streptococcus carbonicus","description":"pretreatment primarily establishes substrate accessibility and precursor availability, whereas indigenous microorganisms facilitate subsequent substrate conversion and functional coordination with exogenous CEB. A two-stage fermentation system integrating different pretreatment strategies with retention or inactivation of indigenous microorganisms was established. The objectives were to: (i) evaluate their effects on MCFAs production and selectivity; (ii) clarify their roles in SCFAs conversion, substrate utilization, and reducing conditions; and (iii) reveal the associated microbial and metabolic mechanisms through community and metagenomic analyses.","center":"Taiyuan University of Technology","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2026/10/22 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN64364814","MIMARKS Survey related sample from sludge metagenome","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2025-06-20",2025,"CN","Shanxi",1793511,"Taiyuan","probable",37.81,112.56,"missing: data agreement-established pre-2023",null,"Sludge microorganism","Anaerobic acclimation","Sludge","city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN64364815","MIMARKS Survey related sample from sludge metagenome","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2025-06-16",2025,"CN","Shanxi",1793511,"Taiyuan","probable",37.81,112.56,"missing: data agreement-established pre-2023",null,"Sludge microorganism","pretreatment","Sludge","city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN64364816","MIMARKS Survey related sample from sludge metagenome","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater"